{
  "dom_id": "step-q90442",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{6}{7}(3x-{x}^{2}),\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{6}{7}(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6}{7}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{6}{7}({x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
